W: 1 My Father, for another night
W: of quiet sleep and rest,
W: for all the joy of morning light,
W: thy holy name be blest.
W:
W: 2 Now with the new-born day I give
W: myself anew to thee,
W: that as thou willest I may live,
W: and what thou willest be.
W:
W: 3 Whate&apos;er I do, things great or small,
W: whate&apos;er I speak or frame,
W: thy glory may I seek in all,
W: do all in Jesus&apos; name.
W:
W: 4 My Father, for his sake, I pray,
W: thy child accept and bless;
W: and lead me by thy grace today
W: in paths of righteousness.</miscellaneous-field>
